Objective: close the review coverage gap around the public read/write path validators and complete the previously blocked native E2E validation.

Decision: do not use the reviewer's direct /etc assertion against the machine policy. Beaver intentionally supports a full-disk policy, including as the compatibility default, so that test would depend on local configuration.

Decision: add a bounded thread-local test policy override. It exercises the real public validate_read_path and validate_write_path functions under a restrictive policy without reading or mutating user configuration and without contaminating parallel tests. The override is compiled only for tests and restored on panic through RAII.

Decision: keep the test utility in its own test-support file and rename read_allows_file_in_working_dir to read_allows_file_in_explicit_root so its name matches the behavior it verifies.

TDD evidence: the new public-validator tests first failed to compile because the isolated policy seam did not exist, then passed after the minimal test-only seam was implemented.

